# QA replay of the stash desk's view (owner, 2026-10-19, from a panel: A1 · B1 · C1 · D2, and the addendum: A(2) · B1 ·
# C1a · Da; step B part 2, the view; step C, 2026-10-19: the card, pinning, the click's copy; owner, 2026-10-25, the
# layout round's decision 1: the GEAR tab mirrored and fixed): the made-up desk (Rules.DeskExample) as readings in the
# menus bring it. The desk takes the map's place by itself in the game's GEAR tab's shape, the POUCH no reading shows a
# dashed frame; its page comes in cell by cell and its totals count up; a window's cell and head light each other; a
# cell's card stands in the rail, with the rule a click copies by; a click copies (its flash, decode and notice; the
# script leaves the clipboard alone); a right-click pins a card; each guard of the copy; a "?" cell's candidates and a
# pick; a reading that showed and changed the backpack alone keeps the rest where it stands, dimmed and dated, and a
# reading that changed nothing changes nothing; PLAN and DESK switch; a raid takes the window and gives it back to Plan,
# the desk keeping its page. A developer build plays it with --dev-view --dev-script; how to run it, and what each still
# must show: desk.md beside this file. Times are in seconds.

# A --dev-view session starts on settings of its own, as at a first start, so the tour opened by itself at chapter 1
# once the data was there. It ends first, and its notice ("The tour stays in help", 6 s) is waited out, so the entry
# still shows the head line counting up, not the notice over it (QA pass of 2026-10-19, F11).
tour end
map customs
wait 7

# The first reading: every region opens, its cells coming in 50 ms apart, the head line counting up.
desk 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\entry
wait 7
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\first

# The Zhuk's cell in the backpack: its window's head and the stem light up; the rail says "One of 2 items".
desk point backpack 0 0
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\window

# The LEDX in the stash: the desk's card in the rail, decision first; its history is the made-up desk's own.
desk point stash 8 0
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\card

# A click on it: its frame flashes gold, its figure decodes, the notice says what was copied and by which rule.
desk copy stash 8 0
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\copy

# The rule on the card, 2 % over: its words and the plate's figure follow, and settings' row with them.
desk rule over:2
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\rule
desk rule under:3

# Two cards pinned (right-clicks): the LEDX, then the Grizzly at 1469/1800 on top; the pointer on to the key past the
# best net, whose card stands first in the rail with the gold light, the two pinned as one line each in the rail's foot,
# in sight under it (UI QA pass of the second round, F1, 2026-10-19). Each pinned cell carries the pin's tab.
desk pin stash 8 0
desk pin backpack 4 1
desk point stash 5 2
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\pinned
# The foot's second line, the LEDX's, clicked: its card whole in the pointed card's place, the Grizzly's line left in the
# foot.
desk show 2
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\pinshown
# Four pinned (the blue keycard and the 5.45 ammo on top), the key pointed at again: three lines in the foot, the fourth,
# the LEDX's, reached by the strip's own scroll.
desk pin pockets 0 0
desk pin rig 5 1
desk point stash 5 2
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\pinmore
desk unpin all

# The guards: the blue keycard Therapist pays more for (a click copies nothing, the notice says why); the 5.45 ammo that
# can't be listed.
desk copy pockets 0 0
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\trader
desk point rig 5 1
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\noflea

# A "?" cell: its card lists the candidates; a click copies nothing and says to pick; the second candidate picked, the
# cell is that item and its card the item's.
desk copy stash 4 1
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\pick
desk pick stash 4 1 2
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\picked

# A reading that showed and changed the backpack alone (a LEDX more): the backpack comes in where it stands, the rest is
# kept in its place, a step dimmer, each head dated; nothing moves.
desk 2
wait 3
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\kept
# The same screenshot again: a reading that changed nothing changes nothing, and dims nothing anew.
desk 3
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\same

# PLAN, then DESK: the map back, then the page as it was.
desk plan
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\plan
desk show
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\show

# A raid loading takes the window, with no click; when it is over, Plan, and DESK shows the page kept. The stills after
# the raid wait out the RAID OVER cue (a still taken while a cue fades fails to render it).
load
steps
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\raid
start
wait 2
end
wait 7
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\after
desk show
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\back
exit
